  "provider_query": "CPython source file that defines PyObject_Malloc",
  "answer": "**`Objects/obmalloc.c`** defines `PyObject_Malloc`.\n\nIt is a thin wrapper that checks the size against `PY_SSIZE_T_MAX` and then calls the current object-domain allocator (`_PyObject.malloc`). The underlying pymalloc implementation (`_PyObject_Malloc` and related helpers) is also in that file when `WITH_PYMALLOC` is enabled.\n\nRelevant sources:\n\n1. **Definition** — `Objects/obmalloc.c` (e.g. around the `PyObject_Malloc` function in recent and 3.12 trees): https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Objects/obmalloc.c  \n2. **Same file, older snapshot** showing `void * PyObject_Malloc(size_t size)`: https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d36cf5f1d20ce9f111a8fc997104785086e8eee6/Objects/obmalloc.c  \n3. **3.12 raw source** of the same function: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.12.0/Objects/obmalloc.c  \n4. **Public declaration / domain docs** — `Include/pymem.h` (object domain: `PyObject_Malloc` / `Realloc` / `Free`): https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d8f0d922d53a8f7bb64c1fda26be386bd2e3d958/Include/pymem.h  \n5. **API docs** — `Doc/c-api/memory.rst` (`.. c:function:: void* PyObject_Malloc(size_t n)`): https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/master/Doc/c-api/memory.rst  \n6. **Internal pymalloc overview** — `Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h`: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/main/Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h  \n7. **Related allocation macros** that call it — `Doc/c-api/allocation.rst` (`PyObject_New` uses `PyObject_Malloc`): https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Doc/c-api/allocation.rst  \n8. **Historical alias cleanup** (`PyObject_MALLOC` → `PyObject_Malloc`) — PR #23587: https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/23587",
